**Read:** MN 101–152 in [The Middle Length Discourses of the Buddha](../sources/Middle-length.lingua#r_7DP0G07DRGWNMD81GH20R1RTNB), completing this division in order. Read the general introduction with the first division and consult notes when an interpretation depends on them.

Complete the collection before moving to the Suttanipāta. Relate meditation, conduct, understanding, and liberation across the whole reading. Modern psychological descriptions can illuminate a comparison when their assumptions remain visible.

**Work through the text:** Choose a meditation instruction and trace its place in the larger discourse and path. Explain its conditions and intended outcome, then compare one scholarly or translational alternative rather than declaring that contemporary vocabulary settles it.

**Check:** locate the passages another reader would need to challenge your reconstruction. Distinguish an example of teaching in context from a rule you have inferred for every possible audience.

**Continue:** [Suttanipāta I–III: poetry, conduct, and renunciation](SNP-First-three.lingua#r_5PVDPVSXQ3WNF32YA1FKQZ4B3G).

